{
  "title": "Medial Epicondylitis (Golfer's Elbow)",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/shoulder-and-elbow/3083/medial-epicondylitis-golfers-elbow",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Feb 29 2024",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Medial Epicondylitis, also know as Golfer's elbow, is an overuse syndrome caused by eccentric overload of the flexor-pronator mass at the medial epicondyle.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made clinically with tenderness around the medial epicondyle made worse with resisted forearm pronation and wrist flexion.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is generally nonoperative with rest, icing, activity modifications and bracing. Rarely, operative management is indicated for patients with persistent symptoms who fail nonoperative management.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "5 to 10 times less common than lateral epicondylitis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "affects men and women equally",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**dominant extremity in 75% of cases**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "age 30s to 60s, most commonly in 30s to 40s.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "risks",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "sports that require repetitive wrist flexion/forearm pronation during ball release",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "common in golfers, baseball pitchers, javelin throwers, bowlers, weight lifters, racquet sports",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "tennis",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "late ball strike (raquet head behind elbow at ball contact)",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "3",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "poor forehand stroke mechanics",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "3",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "failure to use vibration dampeners attached to strings",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "3",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "in athletes, may develop in response to large valgus forces on elbow",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "flexor-pronators reduce force seen by anterior band of medial ulnar collateral ligament (MUCL)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "anterior band MUCL",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "3",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "text": "primary static restraint to valgus force at elbow",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "3",
                              "children": []
                            },
                            {
                              "text": "lies deep to pronator teres and FCR",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "3",
                              "children": []
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "jobs involving lifting >20kg, forceful grip, exposure to constant vibration at elbow (plumbers, carpenters, construction workers)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "can also occur post-traumatically",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "pathoanatomy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "micro-trauma to insertion of flexor-pronator mass caused by repetitive activities",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "traditionally thought to affect pronator teres (PT) > flexor carpi radialis (FCR)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "new studies show all muscles of common flexor tendon (CFT) affected except palmaris longus",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "stages",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "peritendinous inflamation",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "angiofibroblastic hyperplasia",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "breakdown/fibrosis/calcification",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**ulnar neuropathy**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "inflammation may affect ulnar nerve",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**ulnar collateral ligament insufficiency**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "should rule this out, especially in throwing athletes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "associated occupational conditions (present in 84% of occupational medial epicondylitis)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "carpal tunnel syndrome",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "lateral epicondylitis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "rotator cuff tendinitis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Anatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Common flexor tendon (CFT)",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "3 cm long",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "attaches to medial epicondyle (anterior aspect), anterior bundle of MCL",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "fibers run parallel to MCL",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "ulnar head of PT becomes confluent with hyperplastic part of anteromedial joint capsule",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Flexor-pronator mass includes",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3083/images/common%20flexors.jpg",
              "caption": ""
            }
          ],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "pronator teres (median n.)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "flexor carpi radialis (median n.)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "FDS (median n.)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "palmaris longus (median n.)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "flexor carpi ulnaris (ulnar n.)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "History",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "may include acute traumatic blow to elbow causing avulsion of CFT",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "repetitive elbow use, repetitive gripping, repetitive valgus stress",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "+/- numbness or tingling in ulnar digits",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "insidious onset pain over medial epicondyle",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "worse with wrist and forearm motion",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "worse with gripping",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "during late cocking/early acceleration",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "tenderness 5-10 mm distal and anterior to medial epicondyle",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "soft tissue swelling and warmth if inflammation present",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "provocative tests",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "pain with resisted **forearm pronation and wrist flexion**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "examine for associated conditions",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "valgus instability in overhead athlete (milking maneuver, valgus stress, moving valgus stress test)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "ulnar neuritis (2-pt discrimination in ulnar distribution, hypothenar bulk, Tinel's along length of nerve)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "elbow flexion test involves maximal flexion, forearm pronation, wrist hyperextension x 30-60s",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "ulnar subluxation",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "flexion contracture in chronic cases",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "usually unremarkable",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "25% have calcification of CFT or UCL",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "can identify posterior-medial osteophytes or degenerative changes",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "stress radiography used in some centers for assessing valgus instability",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Ultrasound",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "characteristics",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": ">90% sensitivity, specificity, positive and negative predictive values",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "allows dynamic examination",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "hypoechoic/anechoic areas of focal degeneration",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "MRI",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "standard of care",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "indications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "evaluate concomitant pathology (e.g. UCL injury in overhead thrower)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "unclear source of medial elbow pain",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "evaluate for loose bodies",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "rule out rupture of flexor pronator origin",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**tendinosis / tendon disruption of CFT**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "increased signal on T2 images",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3083/images/medial%20epicondylitis.jpg",
                          "caption": "Shows medial epicondylitis"
                        },
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3083/images/medial%20epicondylitis%202.jpg",
                          "caption": ""
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "peritendinous edema",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**UCL or osteochondral injuries**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "EMG/NCS",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "may be used to further evaluate for ulnar nerve compression if identified on history and physical",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Angiofibroblastic hyperplasia, as described for lateral epicondylitis**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Inflammation uncommon**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Differential",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "MCL injury",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "2",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Cubital tunnel syndrome",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "2",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Fracture",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Cervical radiculopathy",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Triceps tendinitis",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Herpes zoster (shingles)",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "rest, ice, activity modification (stop throwing x 6-12wks), PT (passive stretching), bracing, **NSAIDS**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "first line of treatment",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "prolonged trial of conservative management appropriate due to less predictable success of operative treatment (compared to lateral epicondylitis)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "technique",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "counter-force bracing / kinesiology taping",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "ultrasound shown to be beneficial",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "multiple corticosteroid injections should be avoided",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "extracorporeal shockwave therapy (ESWT)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "no definitive recommendations at present",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "promotes angiogenesis, tendon healing, short term analgesia",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "corticosteroid injections into peritendinous tissue",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "complications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "skin depigmentation (if dark skinned)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "subcutaneous atrophy",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "tendon weakening",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "ulnar nerve injury",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "acupuncture",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "open debridement of PT/FCR, reattachment of flexor-pronator group",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**up to 6 months of nonoperative management that fails in a compliant patient**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "symptoms severe and affecting quality of life",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "clear diagnosis",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "outcomes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "good to excellent outcomes in 80% (less than lateral epicondylitis)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "worse outcomes when ulnar nerve symptoms present pre-operatively",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "degree of ulnar neuropathy correlates directly with worse clinical outcomes",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Techniques",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Open debridement and reattachment of flexor-pronator mass**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "approach",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**medial approach to elbow**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "technique",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "use the PT-FCR interval",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "excise regions of pathologic tissue near flexor-pronator mass",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "followed by side-to-side repair at site",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "can perform epicondyle microfracture to enhance vascular environment",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**reattach flexor-pronator mass to medial epicondyle**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**if proximal origin involved**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**can also perform cubital tunnel release or transposition**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**for concomitant ulnar nerve symptoms**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "rehabilitation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "short period of immobilization x 1-2 weeks in sling",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "avoid volar flexion of wrist immediately postoperatively",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "ROM exercises after 2 weeks",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "strengthening at 6-8 weeks",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "return to sport at 3-6 months",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
